==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|au naturel|lit=in the natural}}.

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|head=au naturel|-}}

# [[naturally|Naturally]].
# In the [[plain]]est or simplest manner.
# [[in the nude|In the nude]]: in the [[naked]] state.
#: {{ux|en|Bella loved posing for the artist '''au naturel'''.}}
# Without [[makeup]] and with one's natural hair color.
#* '''2012''', Laura Lascarso, ''Counting Backwards'', Simon and Schuster ({{ISBN|9781442406926}}), page 134:
#*: “Well, few of us are blessed with flawless complexions such as yours, so if you want to go '''au naturel''', that's fine by me.”
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Daryl Wood Gerber|title=Stirring the Plot|year=2014|publisher=Penguin|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=pD5BAwAAQBAJ&lpg=PP1&dq=Stirring%20the%20Plot&hl=es&pg=PP1#v=snippet&q=makeup&f=false|isbn=978-1-101-63759-3|page=121|passage=Why did some women eschew makeup? It seemed to be a recent trend for her. Had her religious fiancé requested she go '''au naturel'''?}}

